    "summary": "The user is probing for the \"standard view\" regarding the economic legacy of 1980s deregulation, specifically asking if the growth-centric supply-side argument has been debunked by more modern, inequality-focused academic literature. The assistant initially provides a balanced overview but progressively shifts toward a specific narrative as the user pushes for a definitive \"winner\" in the academic debate. By the final turn, the assistant concludes that the supply-side dominance has \"significantly waned\" and that few mainstream models favor those gains over social costs.",
